Subject: Install gpgme Python bindings to dist-packages without the setuptools deb scheme
Origin: DHI-internal (DHI build harness)
Description: Keep Debian's dist-packages destination for python3-gpg when the builder setuptools lacks the deb install layout.
Base-Tree: debian gpgme1.0 1.24.2-3
Verify: cmd `dpkg-deb -c python3-gpg_1.24.2-3+deb13u0+dhi0_amd64.deb | grep -E ' \./usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/gpg/__init__\.py$'` expect "dist-packages/gpg/__init__.py"
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI build environment workaround only)
Drop-When: never: DHI builder setuptools has no deb install scheme and Debian setuptools is not pinned in this builder

Debian's 0020 patch passes --install-layout=deb to setup.py install. That option needs the deb scheme from Debian's patched python3-setuptools, but the DHI hermetic builder ships setuptools 84.x without it, so the install step fails with KeyError deb_system. This patch passes the same destination explicitly with --install-purelib and --install-platlib under $(prefix)/lib/python3/dist-packages, so the installed files stay where Debian ships them.

--- a/lang/python/Makefile.am
+++ b/lang/python/Makefile.am
@@ -96,8 +96,10 @@
 	  build \
 	  --build-base="$$(basename "$${PYTHON}")-gpg" \
 	  install \
-	  --install-layout=deb \
 	  --root "$(DESTDIR)" \
+	  --prefix "$(prefix)" \
+	  --install-purelib "$(prefix)/lib/python3/dist-packages" \
+	  --install-platlib "$(prefix)/lib/python3/dist-packages" \
 	  --verbose ; \
 	done
 
